  "note": "A Station's replacement feed after a rollback (Astation #114, items 2 and 6, agreed 2026-11-22, comment 7082464868). station-dev publishes a replacement feed (stations.A2 of the control vectors, a new feed_id) whose snapshot holds svc-discord's cover signed anew (A2_cover) and a current manager's original stop carried as it is: M7_revoke_interrupt, dev-mac's revoke with interrupt_running, which names the old feed (stations.A). The replacement ledger starts with no carried settlement: a fresh ledger, nothing counted. The Station records the snapshot's records (a cover isn't tracked; M7 is, alerted until each of its effects is in force on both covered hosts). host-b had applied M7 from the old feed and reads the replacement feed from 0: its ack names the new feed and its cursor, each of M7's effects a duplicate (the control vectors' Q30); host-c never read the old feed: each effect applied (Q31). Each ack settles M7 on its host: the ledger counts each effect per host through M7 (expect_counts: the ledger's counts, its state's `done`), and once both hosts have both effects in force the re-sign alert ends. The counts survive a restart. The Station admits only acks naming the candidate feed, on sockets opened after the recovery (item 6; the reference ledger checks the origin, never the feed_id, so that rule is the Station's): both links here are such sockets. No Station revoke is recorded, so nothing goes to the Portal.",
